# clinical v1.20 — the canonical narrative spelling, written the way a C-CDA
# section import path is expected to write it from now on.
#
# WHY THIS RECORD. Through v1.19 the reference C-CDA import path wrote a
# section's narrative text to cascade:narrativeText, which core never defines,
# and a second time to clinical:content, which clinical never defines either —
# both predicates sat on nothing a shape targeted. clinical:narrativeText was
# declared the whole time and both JSON-LD contexts already mapped the short
# name narrativeText to it; v1.20 restates its comment as the canonical
# spelling for FHIR Narrative text.div AND C-CDA section text alike, so the
# same property now names both sources rather than the FHIR one only. This
# fixture is that migration's target state: one section narrative, markup
# already stripped by the converter, on the one predicate a reader can rely on.
#
# clinical:documentType carries the human-readable label FHIR R4
# DocumentReference.type.text supplies (clinical:DocumentTypeShape, new in
# v1.20). It is deliberately NOT the closed cascade:documentType slug: the two
# properties hold different values (a label a person reads vs. a short slug
# software branches on) and neither replaces the other.
#
# Exactly one clinical:narrativeText and one clinical:documentType, so neither
# of the two new sh:maxCount 1 Warning shapes (NarrativeTextCountShape,
# DocumentTypeShape) has anything to report here, and neither legacy spelling
# (cascade:narrativeText, clinical:content) is present, so
# NarrativeTextSpellingShape has nothing to report either. All three are new
# in v1.20 and this fixture's claim is that a document written the way the
# release now recommends trips none of them.
#
# Fully synthetic: invented clinic, clinician, visit and section content.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:d0c00116-0000-4000-8000-000000000004> a clinical:ClinicalDocument ;
    clinical:displayName "Progress Note" ;
    clinical:documentType "Progress Note" ;
    clinical:documentDate "2031-04-02"^^xsd:date ;
    clinical:status "final" ;
    clinical:documentReferenceStatus "current" ;

    # One C-CDA section narrative, converted to plain text with the source
    # markup already stripped -- the shape of what a "Plan of Care" section's
    # text element carries.
    clinical:narrativeText "Continue lisinopril 20 mg once daily. Increase walking to 30 minutes five days a week as tolerated. Recheck basic metabolic panel and blood pressure in six weeks. Patient verbalized understanding of the plan and voiced no questions at the close of the visit." ;

    clinical:documentAuthorName "Dara Fennimore, MD" ;
    clinical:fhirResourceId "DocumentReference/dr-56410" ;
    clinical:fhirResourceType "DocumentReference" ;
    clinical:importedAt "2031-04-05T09:40:12-05:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    clinical:sourceEHR "Meridian Health System" ;
    cascade:sourceIdentity "org:meridian" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.4" .
